@Laczen I am trying to understand your suggestions about having one solution for both erase/non-erase device.
Here is a pseudo code of what I understood  in the startup function:
Note that given the fact that NVS at startup doesn't know how the storage was previously written (using erase or using cycle_cnt), it must inquire the flash capabilities first.
```
/* At startup we suppose that the system could be empty and never used */
{
/* search for a closed ATE */
if (flash_params_get_erase_cap & HAS_EXPLICIT_ERASE) {
        look_for_valid_close_ate();
} else {
        look_for_valid_close_ate() && (close_ate.cycle_cnt == first_ate.cycle_cnt)
} 
 /* Now look for an Open ATE */
 if (flash_params_get_erase_cap & HAS_EXPLICIT_ERASE) {
        check_if_ate_equal_fffff()
} else {
        if (look_for_valid_close_ate() && (close_ate.cycle_cnt + 1 == first_ate.cycle_cnt)) => sector open and already used
        else if (close_ate_valid) => sector erased but never used
        else => something went wrong
}
```

> @rghaddab, this PR has been without activity for quite some time. Are you reworking the PR?

@Laczen It is still not clear for me how do you want to merge both algorithms to work on both devices.
I will have a look at this again when I am back from my vacations

